speechtext:
(e)	When any loss of life occurs by reason of any casualty happening to or on board any boat belonging to a fishing or other vessel registered in Canada;
(f)	When any British ship is lost or supposed to have been lost and any evidence is obtainable in Canada as to the circumstances under which she proceeded to sea or was last heard of.
It does not matter where the casualty has occurred, if the evidence is obtainable in Canada by the Merchant's Shipping Act of 1894, they have power to investigate. But they suggest that we should take it up here, the evidence being obtainable here.
